Hermes, this is a required template-level update for the reusable OpenMontage talking-head review pipeline. Please treat the RFC block as the rule set and the JSON block as the target config state. This is not clip-specific creative feedback; it is a default template behavior update for future talking-head review exports.

====================
RFC PATCH
====================

PATCH_TYPE: REQUIRED_TEMPLATE_UPDATE
PROJECT: OpenMontage
TARGET_TEMPLATE: talking_head_reviewable_square_subtitled
INTENT: make the current proof-of-concept into the default clean review asset path for future talking-head clips sourced from long-form video

CURRENT_STATE
- Review outputs currently exist in multiple variants, including square without subtitles, non-square, square subtitled, and square subtitled with large hook overlay
- Preferred direction is square subtitled
- Large hook overlay variant is less preferred because it occupies too much frame real estate
- Subtitle placement appears too central for talking-head framing and can interfere with face visibility

REQUIRED_CHANGES
1. Default output format
- Set default reviewable export for talking-head clips to 1080x1080
- Set default aspect ratio to 1:1
- Keep burned subtitles enabled by default

2. Subtitle placement
- Move subtitle vertical placement from center / mid-frame to lower-third
- Target subtitle anchor at 0.76 Y from top of frame
- Acceptable operating range: 0.75 to 0.78 Y from top
- Maintain bottom safe margin for platform UI avoidance
- Subtitle block must avoid the speaker mouth / chin / central face area

3. Hook overlay default
- Disable large hook overlay by default
- Do not place hook text in the central frame area
- Default hook behavior should be the spoken opening + burned subtitles
- If a hook overlay is explicitly requested, it must render only as a minimal top-bar treatment

4. Framing behavior
- Preserve current square crop behavior unless face-safe recentering is needed
- Allow talking-head-safe recentering when required
- Subtitle position must remain lower-third even if crop center changes
- Do not tie subtitle placement to exact crop center

5. Template scope
- Apply these settings as default template behavior for future talking-head review exports
- Do not treat this as a manual one-off adjustment for only the current clip set

DO_NOT_CHANGE
- Do not redesign subtitle style unless necessary
- Do not change subtitle readability characteristics if current style is already working
- Do not replace square output with vertical output for this template
- Do not reintroduce large hook overlay as a default behavior

EXPORT_REQUIRED
- Render one fresh review export from an existing talking-head proof clip
- Output must use:
  - 1080x1080 square
  - burned subtitles
  - subtitle Y = 0.76 from top
  - large hook overlay disabled
- Return this export as the new baseline review candidate

ACCEPTANCE_CRITERIA
- Speaker face is not materially blocked by subtitle lines
- Subtitle readability remains strong on mobile
- Result is visually cleaner than the current large-hook variant
- Result is suitable as the default reusable reviewable template for talking-head source clips

IMPLEMENTATION_PRIORITY
1. subtitle position
2. hook overlay default behavior
3. framing safety validation
4. fresh baseline export

